  ],
  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "048bba3c2a2240778441affc6cc52d3d_26",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 38 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 sets out the powers of Food Safety Officer."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1dd1097e58b24b7e97f0e5f6c1bc415b_27",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is as follows :\n38. Powers of Food Safety Officer."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7477b252d10c4618a2cb4b50c2c085ae_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(1) The Food Safety Officer may  (a) take a sample  (i) of any food, or any substance, which appears to him to be intended for sale, or to have been sold for human consumption; or (ii) of any article of food or substance which is found by "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3518ee67eb5043daa1a52cff0ded62b7_30",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(8) Where any books of account or other documents are seized under sub-section (6),\nthe Food Safety Officer shall, within a period not exceeding thirty days from the date of seizure, return the same to the person from whom they were seized"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "224934974d44493bb30b73d49d723dc5_31",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Provided that where such person refuses to so certify and a prosecution has been instituted against him under this Act, such books of account or other documents shall be returned to him only after copies thereof and extracts there from as c"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9687f20f015b4ad8b92b248f53940fdb_32",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(9) When any adulterant is seized under sub-section (6), the burden of proving that such adulterant is not meant for purposes https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis of adulteration shall be on the person from whose possession such adulterant was "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0e6fb30867f7470297e1df1fe84ff670_33",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(10) The Commissioner of Food Safety may from time to time issue guidelines with regard to exercise of powers of the Food Safety Officer, which shall be binding:\nProvided that the powers of such Food Safety Officer may also be revoked for "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6242b7ae0dc84b2992ce2c7dce6de1f2_34",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is relevant to note that the provisions in the Act do not empower the official concerned to seal the premises where the contraband has been allegedly kept."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "537603fb59254118ae684f31451fb74c_35",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe power to seal is conferred by Rule 2.1.3..4 (i) of the Food Safety and Standard Rules, 2011."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "86f60618a6e6481fbad962c83d0aeaa3_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The said provision reads as follows :\n4.Powers and Duties: (i) Without prejudice to the powers conferred on him under section 38 of the Act, where the Food Safety Officer is of the opinion or he has reason(s) to be recorded in writing that "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9d910b79a42541b986fed3ac361b3cde_37",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 91 of the Act empowers the Central Government to make rules."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2d7956916da94381a08719f8307303ec_38",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The 2011 Rules have been issued only pursuant to the said power."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "105001cd56d242159abd25c6ecf7f3bf_39",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 91 of the Act is as follows :\n91.Power of Central Government to make rules."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b110a571ba004ecda5e564fef913a69c_40",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(1) The Central Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, make rules for carrying out the provisions of this Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bcc59e4b7b984adf88b62961b81cf38b_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(2) In particular, and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing power, such rules may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:-\nNagoorkani vs The Commissioner on 2 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankano"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8262862bc5a74898830dbe2556abd70c_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, Rule 2.1.3..4(i) will have to be justified only in terms of Section 91(1) of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1c7548ed102c4933b8e41513ba1c8191_43",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt is well settled that a subordinate legislation must conform to the provisions of the parent statute."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0cf43d74abca485db458e1ee780f0811_44",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe rules can never travel beyond the provisions set out in the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6a19e865b21a4c41b6f32b3d16ce319d_45",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 91(1) envisages framing of rules for the purpose of carrying out the provisions https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5d1da9adf40a400db3c08b1cd3b551a1_46",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This power cannot be exercised in such a way as to bring into existence substantive rights or obligations or disabilities not contemplated by the parent Act itself."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a185eb9f2a0c4b239ea2cb297e44a8fe_47",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Laghu Udhyog Bharti it has Nagoorkani vs The Commissioner on 2 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/144795267/\n5 been held that when the Act confers rule making power for carrying out purposes of the Act, rules canno"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "68ef3f67d0914ef1ac607ffead0cd5bb_48",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The legal effect of the formula is to confer a plenary power on the delegate to make rules subject to the overall requirement that the rules made ought to have a nexus with the purpose of the Act (MP Jain & SN Jain on Principles of Administ"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3f842fb07fd8469fbbfb065a2611a3a3_49",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n6.Rule 2.1.3..4(i) refers to Section 38 of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "00b34a563ed84d348520b51eb9d2c82e_50",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 38 of the Act empowers the Food Safety Officer to take a sample and seize any article of food that appears to be in contravention of the Act or the regulations made thereunder."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bf8b511c995f4f639d82fe2b0b54a1a7_51",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Foot Safety Officer can also keep the seized food article in the safe custody of the Food Business Operator after taking a sample."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6fd8a7fa86944ede962641a3c9541fc0_52",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Food Business Operator may also be required to execute a bond for a sum of money equal to the value of the seized article with one or more sureties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f82a7e2a6f2c47ba8145edcdc44e2b6e_53",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Only if the Food Safety Officer is of the opinion that Section 38(1)(c) or the proviso to Section 38(1) could not be complied with, the premises can be sealed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9a67f3ae7400459994f084aeded5c130_54",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Rule itself contemplates one such situation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8be26d789dbf45c494b3929a8869d923_55",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If the Food Business Operator is https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis not available, then, the seized article cannot be kept in his safe custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "688c4890e60b439b8252bed5be13f826_56",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is only under such circumstances sealing is permissible."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "67df32a87ac84653b73f85dfd7f9bded_57",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The second respondent has not complied with the statutory requirement set out in the Rule."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8a591131060648bdbf4ce95e6717649c_58",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The power of sealing is a drastic one and it cannot be expansively construed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3b2231be2b7d4dd189a147da9095fcd5_59",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This is all the more so because in the parent Act, there is no provision for sealing."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b006e647103e4de58caa9b088de9eb8f_60",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Rules have been framed only to carry out the provisions of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1f384aa711074a46a7b966f29e8c2a09_61",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 38 (1)(c) of the Act refers to the safe custody of the seized article."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fe1beb6f079044c39c631c57fa8f79c2_62",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Sealing can be done only if the mode set out in the parent Act cannot be fulfilled."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9daf8959e40241f6833344dabf8dd74e_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Rule 2.1.3..4 should be understood in the light of Section 91(1) of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6ee5a237eba84147b2c28ff3364f02b4_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n7.In the instant case, it is not the case of the respondents that the petitioner was not available."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "013f029d79f640a19158a91e3cf3aa63_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not their case that the procedure set out in Section 38(1)(c) of the Act could not be fulfilled."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0646dbd8f9944796879805e1140c271c_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nTherefore, the sealing of the petitioners' premises appears to be unwarranted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "25c38cf08e794a0c813dfe310f37a2a8_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n8.The issue can be approached from yet another angle."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4593a4d0e52b4ae4bae4481b3df86c7a_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in the decision reported in (2022) 3 SCC 694 (Akshay N Patel v. RBI)"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ace002969813443baee7d2936b4e999f_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "reiterated the proportionality standard in determining violations of fundamental rights."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "84a0cc1658a04965869e35e43029a69e_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The four-pronged approach laid down in Aadhar case was approvingly cited."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8e9c01463d7646aaacb98fe018cfa7b0_71",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The test is as follows :\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 319."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "825aed42688f4b75a0d7c96df72b0746_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": " This discussion brings out that following four subcomponents of proportionality need to be satisfied:\n319.1. A measure restricting a right must have a legitimate goal (legitimate goal stage).\n319.2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6353e173c7904f03bc2d70c38adc4632_73",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It must be a suitable means of furthering this goal (suitability or rational connection stage)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b56b798e3b1c4f93ba2b110b9fcf2971_74",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n319.3. There must not be any less restrictive but equally effective alternative (necessity stage)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0c99a48f047d4346b18fd73d26ba97f0_75",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nNagoorkani vs The Commissioner on 2 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/144795267/\n6 319.4."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "532ddcedfa9244dda03380d7d29e509f_76",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The measure must not have a disproportionate impact on the right holder (balancing stage)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "37fe8368dff9467886d1557e8c7e24d1_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The doctrine of proportionality can be invoked to test the validity of an executive action."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "36290f21a13f4defad1cc8cc2f7ae66a_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In this case, the seized articles could have been left in the safe custody of the petitioners."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d5d3112c06f24c98a5bd44266623f087_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This is contemplated by the Act itself."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8047ed0f1dfe4fdd8cbcfa5828a0467d_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Instead, the second respondent resorted to sealing the premises itself."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cca11e01df784b48bed246b4ddcff046_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The act of the second respondent fails the test laid down in the third prong."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0c249b66630e4e1b828f9ae2e9010163_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The sealing was done on 16.12.2023."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "140cdc50113442a5b8ee8e7c69cfcafc_83",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "More than two weeks have passed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "00d57b1e5e3c4aada588c3153202ff89_84",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The petitioners are small time shop keepers."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "399b34a05daf4a459c2c2b07251ca12a_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Right to carry on business is guaranteed under Article 19(1)(g) of the Constitution of India."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "abbe0654348d4f62b74384f5c239b0fe_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Of course, there is no right to trade in banned items."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b3eb3709a588449796dd3bd49617f6be_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "But the petitioners can sell other products in their shops."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ab4c2cd8a4ed40cd8ef6cc8b0b632c0a_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "By sealing the shop, the petitioners' right to livelihood is affected."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ebd1ce7b54134434a75525ae5539d467_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This will have a disproportionate impact on the petitioners' rights."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "05814de3b0a647f99ad60cb0652dfa79_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In any event, by keeping the shops closed, the investigation in this case is not going to be https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis advanced."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "88166427135947f9886e972402800f88_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If the shops are ordered to be opened,\nthe investigation will not suffer."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fdf42d9852c2414b9ad62e154e5b94e8_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not necessary that the premises should continue to remain closed as that may not serve any purpose."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "60e243fd659940208ce45268799b5783_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even if there is justification in initially sealing the premises, at some point of time or the other, they have to be de sealed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2bd452788b354bc3a1244937d0e8a8e4_94",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Merely for the reason that banned tobacco products were kept for sale, a shop cannot be closed forever."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "42ce56eeb9474a35b9cc6ec6ca32309b_95",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That is why, the Rules provide for sealing the premises only for one reason ie., inability to adhere to the procedure contemplated in Section 38(1)(c) of the Act or the proviso thereto."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e54769876c8244ff92821f822338652d_96",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n9.Considering the impact on the petitioners' livelihood, the respondents are directed to de seal the petition-mentioned premises forthwith."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b0a53a765bbf461fbfcf3db1af62149d_97",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The petitioners are directed to file affidavits before this Court undertaking not to trade in any banned items including tobacco products."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3effe115b66047e1b1364dc131cba803_98",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If the undertaking is breached, consequences will follow."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2d918a8885bd49669dd4c664315e3f4d_99",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The writ petitions are allowed on these terms."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6d8a136351914a8ab733df3f7eba0b10_100",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No costs."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f126f530ffd44b7c97dad485c0ebf60b_101",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nConnected miscellaneous petitions are closed."
    }
  ],
